WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.200
- All right. Let's end this off

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.810
with one last feel-good story.

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:04.390
This is 'What I'm Liking'

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:06.478
(upbeat music plays)

00:00:06.478 --> 00:00:10.160
A man known as Bayou Dave's on
a mission to save the world.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.370
At least the bayou anyway.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.430
Five days a week, he
combs Houston Waterway

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:16.490
scoopin' up seemingly
endless pockets of trash

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:18.410
that's destroying the area's ecosystem.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.850
And to prove just how bad
the situation has become,

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.873
he makes videos like this for
the world to see. Take a look.

00:00:23.873 --> 00:00:24.706
(transition effect whooshes)

00:00:24.706 --> 00:00:26.510
- [Dave] This is called a turnin' base.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.850
We have to do something
about this, people.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.933
Am I the only one that
wants to save the world?

00:00:38.839 --> 00:00:40.839
Bayou Dave, signin' out!

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.610
- Well, we have him on the line right now

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.870
from Buffalo Bayou
Partnership, let's say hello

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:47.770
to Bayou Dave.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:50.410
Dave, how are you, my friend?
(audience member cheers)

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:51.920
- Hey, Jay. How you doin'?

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.430
- This is like your
life mission, isn't it?

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:56.580
- Yes, this is my life's mission.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.200
I've been at Buffalo Bayou
Partnership for 12 years

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.170
and since I've been here,

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.520
I've had the opportunity to be able to

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.410
save the world.
- [Jay] Yeah.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:10.210
- I never knew how bad the
pollution was until I got here.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.760
And since I've been here,

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.260
we've added containment booms,

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:19.330
and we've gotten 12 dump
trucks of trash per week,

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.530
from the bayou.
- [Jay] Wow.

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:24.030
- [Dave] We feel like this is
important to save the world

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.250
and other people need to know about it.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.940
- [Jay] Now, why is
this work in this video

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.660
so important to you?

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.180
- Because I realized people

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.660
just don't know.
- [Jay] Yeah.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.300
- They just don't know that
the trash is out there.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:39.610
And it hit a soft spot with
me when I saw all the animals

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:41.680
that were affected by the trash.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:43.150
We have,

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.700
the snake population was
down when I got here.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:50.880
Turtles, the osprey,
it was only one osprey.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.660
One neighboring osprey when I got here.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:55.900
Now we have four or five breeding pairs.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:59.170
So we know that the water
quality is getting a lot better.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:02.330
And we know that if we don't
do something, no one will

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:05.700
and Buffalo Bayou Partnership
is a non-profit organization

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.610
so there's some things we
put together with duct tape

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.830
and bubble gum, but we
do whatever we need to do

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.290
to try to make it work.
Failure's not an option.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.360
- [Jay] Well, that's great.
And maybe the politicians

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.854
will come in to try to save
their fellow snakes, you know?

00:02:17.854 --> 00:02:19.031
(audience members exclaim)
'Cause they have,

00:02:19.031 --> 00:02:20.450
(Dave laughs)
they got, you know,

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.000
well, they got something in common.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.080
They see their own brethren in there and

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.790
they're, "Oh! We gotta save this bayou!"

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.210
So let's get those politicians
- Jay.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:29.670
- No, you can't be
shaking your head, Dave.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.110
Yeah, okay.
(audience members laugh)

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:33.140
Well, that's great, my friend.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:34.540
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:35.990
Keep up the good work, my friend.

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:36.823
We applaud you.
(Jay claps)

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.330
Thank you so much for what you do.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:39.960
And that's not all. Our
season-long partners,

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.370
Pilot Pen, makers of G-2, the go-to pen

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.600
of The Kelly Clarkson Show wanna honor

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.760
ultimate overachievers
like this gentleman.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.228
So, they're writing you
a cheque for $1,000.

00:02:49.228 --> 00:02:50.120
(audience members applaud)
So thank you very much, Dave.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.150
(Jay claps)
Congratulations, buddy.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:53.069
There you go.

00:02:53.069 --> 00:02:53.902
(Jay claps)
- Appreciate it, Jay.

00:02:53.902 --> 00:02:55.550
- [Jay] There you go,
you got it, my friend!

